don't know on on that bill bill gates  posited this idea of creative capitalism  in which he broadened the the notion  that the one can have an ethical company  and a company can i play a broader role  than just profit maximization for  shareholders and in that way we can  actually see multiple returns to society  beyond you know the the great product  that the company makes or for the  shareholder money that they will give as  a residual because that's their money to  give but the company itself can be  ethical and have an impact but a lot of  people oppose that view and say no  companies should be limited to profit  maximization sort of in the friedman  sense do you agree with that I think  profit maximization is really a too  narrow of a definition in the role the  company I might say I'm more on Bill  Gates aside on this that you know the  company is is a member of the community  in some sense and needs to play a role  in the broad broadly defined community  and you know you have to be careful  about it because certainly you have to  pay attention to profits and investors  is one very key element of that  community because if you don't pay  attention to them they're not going to  keep financing your company and you're  not going to have a company and all your  wonderful things for employees are going  to go away so I think you know it's a  balancing act it's all about being  balanced but I think that part of that  balance is are those other  constituencies so I don't understand the  notion of taking one constituency  investors and putting them way above all  of those other constituencies to me that  that's not doesn't make sense  intellectually but it also doesn't make  sense for the long-term health of the  company i think the long-term health of  a company will be far better if the  company is trying to balance all those  constituencies having a great place for  employees to work for example you can  say investors would be better served if  you try to pay people the lowest  possible amount but i think in the end  investors are better served if the  employees are happy  and thriving and building careers and  enjoying themselves and being creative  and innovative so you know it all plays  together it's very complex
 

